<task id="105" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>CommunicationConnections PCF — UX rebuild: group by action, plain-language statuses, explicit per-row controls (UAT R2 C1)</title>
    <phase>Wave 10 — UAT round 2 refinements</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>8</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>042,043</dependencies>
    <blocks>—</blocks>
    <tags>pcf, frontend, fluent-ui, dataverse</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Reworks a shipped PCF's UX + interaction model (.tsx); PCF build+pack+deploy. Code-review + adr-check.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W10</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-17</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    UAT round 2 C1 (`notes/UAT-ROUND2-FEEDBACK.md`): the CommunicationConnections modal is confusing — "I'm still
    not clear on how I'm supposed to resolve, or what the statuses mean." The MATCHING is correct (verified: subject
    matter+project, body matter → Ambiguous, sender contact filed); the problem is the UI/interaction.

    OWNER-APPROVED redesign (mockup: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/3c1eaf58-8b56-4417-9819-0a1aed1dace7 —
    rendered from the real "CMRCL-848992 Smith v Smith" email). Rebuild the modal to GROUP BY ACTION NEEDED, not by
    record type:
      1. "Needs your decision" — Ambiguous conflicts as selectable options + a "Set as primary" action.
      2. "Filed automatically" — high-confidence auto-links, marked done, with the ★ primary clearly shown +
         change/unlink.
      3. "Suggested" — soft matches (AI, name matches, and the new B1 contacts) each with explicit Confirm ✓ /
         Dismiss ✕.
    Replace the opaque "Ambiguous / Primary / Filed / Suggested" chips with plain-language actions + a status
    LEGEND. Each row states exactly what to do (pick-a-matter radio, Set as primary, Confirm, Dismiss).

    Rebuild the presentation/interaction of the existing `CommunicationConnections` PCF
    (`src/client/pcf/CommunicationConnections/`) — it reads `sprk_associationprovenance` (candidates + statuses)
    and `sprk_associationstatus`, and writes the additive typed-lookup regarding fields (per the task-042 engine
    map). Keep the data contract; change the UX + the resolve interactions to match the approved mockup.
  </prompt>

  <goal>
    The Connections modal groups matches by action (Needs decision / Filed / Suggested), uses plain-language
    verbs + a legend instead of opaque status chips, and gives each row one explicit control — so a reviewer knows
    exactly how to resolve conflicts and confirm/dismiss suggestions. Data contract (provenance in, regarding
    writes out) unchanged.
  </goal>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Matches render in three action-grouped sections: "Needs your decision" (conflicts), "Filed automatically" (auto-linked), "Suggested" (confirm/dismiss) — driven off the provenance candidates + statuses.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A conflict (Ambiguous field) renders as selectable options with a "Set as primary" action that writes the chosen target to the regarding field (using the existing additive typed-lookup write path from task 042).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Suggested rows (AI create-suggestions, name matches, B1 contacts) each have explicit Confirm (link/create) and Dismiss controls; Filed rows show the ★ primary + change/unlink.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A plain-language status legend is present; opaque bare-chip statuses are replaced by action verbs (per the mockup).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The provenance-read + regarding-write DATA CONTRACT is unchanged (only presentation/interaction reworked); existing 042 write semantics (additive, never clear-and-set) preserved.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Fluent v9 tokens only, theme-correct light + dark (ADR-021); matches the Spaarke system style (reuse the 101 design-standards header/row spec where applicable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build:prod` clean; jest for the grouping + resolve/confirm/dismiss interactions; version bump all 5 locations (→ 1.1.0); solution ZIP repacked + validated (type-66; manifest generic + apostrophe-free).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <constraints>
    <constraint>Do NOT change the association DATA model or the engine — this is a client UX rebuild over the existing `sprk_associationprovenance` / `sprk_associationstatus` contract.</constraint>
    <constraint>Preserve task-042 write semantics: multi-association = additive typed-lookup writes mirroring the engine's RegardingFieldMap; never clear-and-set.</constraint>
    <constraint>ADR-028 auth (`@spaarke/auth`, authReady gate, no PublicClientApplication); ADR-021 Fluent v9 tokens; ADR-022 virtual control + platform libs.</constraint>
    <constraint>Manifest description-keys generic + apostrophe-free (R2 XSD fix); solution = type-66 only; follow /pcf-deploy.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <notes>
    Mockup is the source of truth for layout/labels/interaction: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/3c1eaf58-8b56-4417-9819-0a1aed1dace7
    Read the existing `CommunicationConnections` components (ConnectionsEditor + provenance parsing) first — reuse
    the provenance model + write path; only the presentation layer changes. Depends on B1 (102) for the contact
    suggestions to appear in the "Suggested" section, but the UX rebuild can proceed independently (contacts just
    populate when 102 ships). Deploy remainder (import) = owner.
  </notes>
</task>
